cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "calendar_letf: calendar-reset versus daily-reset leveraged funds"
version: 0.1.1
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "calendar_letf contributors"
abstract: >-
  A tested engine that models calendar-reset leveraged funds from 1x to 3x (weekly, monthly and quarterly resets with
  an early reset) against daily-reset twins at identical costs on the S&P 500, the Nasdaq-100 and the semiconductor
  index. It validates the model against live calendar-reset ETFs and monthly-reset mutual funds, chooses leverage with
  intervals, runs block-bootstrap Monte Carlo, and tests timing rules without look-ahead. THEORY.md gives the
  mathematics, each formula tied to its code and a test. Research tooling, not investment advice.
keywords:
  - leveraged ETF
  - calendar reset
  - volatility drag
  - backtest
